  "term": "crystallization",
  "definition": "Crystallization is the formation of an ordered crystal from a purified substance in a supersaturated solution under conditions that encourage molecules to associate. In this context, it is a sought-after but uncommon outcome of laboratory trials, distinct from amorphous precipitation or no visible change.",
